{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Except Caleb son of Jephunneh.</b> And if you ask: did not Jair son of Manasseh too enter the land, and he was killed at Ai, as we say there: 'thirty-six men' — this is Jair son of Manasseh, who was equivalent to the majority of the Sanhedrin; and in this very portion too it is said, 'ויאיר בן מנשה הלך וילכוד את חוותיהם' (and Jair son of Manasseh went and captured their villages)? One may answer: the decree was not decreed upon those less than twenty years old and upon those more than fifty, for those less than twenty and more than fifty do not go out to the army. Perhaps Jair son of Manasseh was, at the time of the decree, over fifty."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:29.326193870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}